---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import InquiryDialog from '../components/InquiryDialog.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="OEM / ODM Partnership | TRAKNOVA"
  description="OEM and ODM cooperation for industrial mobility: private label, configured rugged devices and project development, from prototype to mass production."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">OEM / ODM PARTNERSHIP</span>
        <h1>Your brand.<br /><em>Our engineering commitment.</em></h1>
        <p>From a branded variant of an existing platform to a project-specific device, TRAKNOVA supports distributors, solution providers and brands building their own industrial mobility portfolio.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <button class="button button-accent" data-inquiry-open>Discuss Your Project ↗</button>
          <a class="button button-glass" href={withBase('/products/')}>View Platforms ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">ENGAGEMENT MODELS</span>
            <h2>Choose the depth<br />of partnership.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Not every partner needs a new device. Start from where you are: an existing platform to brand, a configuration to adapt, or a product to develop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="model-grid">
          <article class="model-card">
            <span class="model-kicker">MODEL 01</span>
            <h3>Private label</h3>
            <p>Bring an existing platform to market under your brand, with your identity on the device and the packaging.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Logo, boot animation and wallpapers</li>
              <li>Packaging and documentation branding</li>
              <li>Accessory branding</li>
              <li>Regional configuration and serialization</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="model-best">Best for distributors and brands with an existing product plan.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="model-card featured">
            <span class="model-kicker">MODEL 02 <span class="model-badge">MOST COMMON</span></span>
            <h3>Configured product</h3>
            <p>Adapt the platform to your application, market and software environment before it reaches your customers.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Barcode, RFID, NFC or ID module selection</li>
              <li>Memory, OS and accessory configuration</li>
              <li>Software image, preload and MDM enrollment</li>
              <li>Pilot build and acceptance testing</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="model-best">Best for solution providers with a defined use case.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="model-card">
            <span class="model-kicker">MODEL 03</span>
            <h3>Project development</h3>
            <p>Define, prototype and industrialize a device around a requirement that the standard range does not cover.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Requirement and market definition</li>
              <li>Industrial design and prototype coordination</li>
              <li>Validation plan and field pilot</li>
              <li>Pilot production, mass production and lifecycle support</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="model-best">Best for partners with a differentiated device roadmap.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="note-line">Final scope, minimum order quantity, lead time and commercial terms are confirmed per project after configuration review.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">CUSTOMIZATION MATRIX</span>
            <h2>What can be<br />adapted.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The matrix below is a working starting point. Each item is reviewed against the selected platform, the target market and the production plan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="matrix-wrap">
          <table class="matrix-table custom-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Options to discuss</th><th>Status</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Brand identity</td><td>Logo, boot animation, wallpapers, device labels, packaging, manuals</td><td><span class="status-pill accent">Project-defined</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Capture modules</td><td>1D / 2D scan engine, UHF RFID, NFC, ID / document reader</td><td><span class="status-pill">SKU-dependent</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Compute &amp; memory</td><td>Android or Windows variant, RAM / storage, processor option</td><td><span class="status-pill">SKU-dependent</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>I/O &amp; connectivity</td><td>RS232 / RS485, RJ45, USB, HDMI, cellular and Wi-Fi options</td><td><span class="status-pill">SKU-dependent</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Accessories</td><td>Chargers, cradles, grips, cases, straps, vehicle mounts</td><td><span class="status-pill">Tooling-dependent</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Software</td><td>OS image, preloaded applications, MDM enrollment, regional settings</td><td><span class="status-pill accent">Project-defined</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Documentation</td><td>Datasheet, user manual, quick guide, packaging artwork</td><td><span class="status-pill accent">Project-defined</span></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Production</td><td>Serialization, QC plan, packaging, spares planning</td><td><span class="status-pill accent">Project-defined</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="note-line">Availability is confirmed against the selected platform. Some options require tooling, minimum quantities or certification review.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">COOPERATION PROCESS</span>
            <h2>From first conversation<br />to mass production.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Each stage has a defined output and an acceptance point. We do not move to the next gate until both sides agree the previous one is closed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-grid">
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Discovery</h3>
            <p>Application, target market, expected volume, compliance requirements and commercial expectations are discussed in one structured intake.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Proposal</h3>
            <p>Recommended platform or development path, configuration, branding scope, MOQ and a stage-by-stage commercial framework.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Prototype</h3>
            <p>Sample build with the agreed branding, software image and accessory set. Open issues are recorded for the validation stage.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Validation</h3>
            <p>Test plan, field pilot and acceptance criteria. Documentation and outstanding engineering items are closed before pilot production.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Pilot production</h3>
            <p>Pre-production run to confirm process, packaging, serialization and QC. Both sides sign off on the production baseline.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="process-step">
            <h3>Production &amp; support</h3>
            <p>Mass production against the approved baseline, with spares planning, documentation control and after-sales coordination.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="process-note">Sample policy, MOQ, lead time and tooling terms are defined in the proposal for the specific project.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">QUALITY &amp; DOCUMENTATION</span>
            <h2>Built into the project,<br />not inspected at the end.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The applicable test plan, acceptance criteria and document package are agreed during the proposal. Certification scope depends on the target market and device configuration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quality-grid">
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Quality approach</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Incoming material checks</li>
              <li>In-process checks</li>
              <li>Final inspection</li>
              <li>Test records retained per batch</li>
              <li>Packaging and label verification</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Document package</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Product datasheet</li>
              <li>User manual and quick guide</li>
              <li>Packaging artwork</li>
              <li>Test and conformity documentation where available</li>
              <li>Change-control records</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Lifecycle support</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Spares planning</li>
              <li>Accessory continuity</li>
              <li>Software image control</li>
              <li>Change notification</li>
              <li>After-sales coordination</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">OEM / ODM FAQ</span>
            <h2>Questions partners<br />ask first.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>If your question is not covered here, include it in the project inquiry. We will answer it against the specific platform and market.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>Can we put our logo on the device and packaging?</summary>
            <p>Yes, within the scope agreed for the project. Logo application, boot animation, labels, packaging and manuals are reviewed together because they affect tooling, minimum quantities and artwork approval.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What is the minimum order quantity?</summary>
            <p>It depends on the platform, configuration and branding scope. Private-label projects usually have a different threshold from full project development. The MOQ is defined in the proposal after the requirement review.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can you preload our application and MDM profile?</summary>
            <p>Software image and preload can be discussed as part of the configured-product model. The exact scope — preload list, MDM enrollment, regional settings and update responsibility — is documented before prototyping.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do you support regional RFID bands and approvals?</summary>
            <p>UHF RFID frequency bands and market approvals differ by country. We confirm the target market before selecting the module and include the applicable configuration in the proposal.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can we receive samples before a production order?</summary>
            <p>Sample policy and lead time are agreed per project. For configured products, a prototype or pilot build is the usual acceptance step before mass production.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Who owns tooling and documentation?</summary>
            <p>Ownership, change notification and documentation rights are defined in the project agreement. We recommend agreeing these before tooling or artwork is released.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What certifications can you support?</summary>
            <p>Certification scope depends on the target market, the device configuration and the applicable standard. We review the requirement during discovery and align the document package accordingly.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap cta-band">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">START A CONVERSATION</span>
          <h2>Bring us your<br />requirement.</h2>
          <p>Tell us the application, target market, expected volume and branding scope. We will come back with the right platform and a project path.</p>
        </div>
        <button class="button button-accent" data-inquiry-open>Discuss Your Project ↗</button>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer /><InquiryDialog />
</BaseLayout>
